@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+{
+  "file": "src/flows.ts",
+  "snippet": "tags: z.string().describe('Up to three lowercase topic tags, comma separated'),",
+  "cause": "The TicketSummarySchema declares tags as a single string and asks for comma-separated text, so the model returns one string like \"shipping, damage\" instead of a list of tags.",
+  "evidence": "src/flows.ts line 8 defines tags as z.string() with the description 'Up to three lowercase topic tags, comma separated', and summarizeTicket uses this schema as its structured output schema (output: { schema: TicketSummarySchema }) and returns it unchanged, so the flow's output contains the comma-joined string the dashboard receives. No other code in the repo splits or converts tags. The fix changes the field to z.array(z.string()), and tsc --noEmit passes. I did not call the live model, so the end-to-end result was not reproduced."
+}
